{"name":"Smoke and Mirrors","hex":"#d9e6e8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"smoke and mirrors","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deceptive, fraudulent, or unconvincing explanation or description."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smoke_and_mirrors"}],"entries":[{"title":"Smoke and Mirrors (Gaiman book)","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke and Mirrors: Short Fictions and Illusions is a collection of short stories and poems by English writer Neil Gaiman. It was first published in the United States in 1998, and in the United Kingdom in 1999. The UK edition included five stories not in the US edition, four of which were included in the US edition of the other collection Fragile Things."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/01/Ngsmam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke_and_Mirrors_(Gaiman_book)"},{"title":"Smoke and Mirrors (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke and Mirrors is 2008 crime novel by Australian author Kel Robertson. It won the 2009 Ned Kelly Award for Best Fiction. It is the second novel in the author's series about Australian Chinese Federal Police detective Brad Chen."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d1/Smoke_and_Mirrors_%28novel%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke_and_Mirrors_(novel)"},{"title":"Smoke and mirrors","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke and mirrors is a classic technique in magical illusions that makes an entity appear to hover in empty space. It was documented as early as 1770 and spread widely after its use by the charlatan Johann Georg Schröpfer, who claimed to conjure spirits. It subsequently became a fixture of 19th-century phantasmagoria shows. The illusion relies on a hidden projector whose beam reflects off a mirror into a cloud of smoke, which in turn scatters the beam to create an image."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9c/1770_Guyot_-_Nouvelles_r%C3%A9cr%C3%A9ations_physiques_et_math%C3%A9matiques.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke_and_mirrors"},{"title":"Smoke","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke is an aerosol emitted when a material undergoes combustion or pyrolysis, together with the quantity of air that is entrained or otherwise mixed into the mass. It is commonly an unwanted by-product of fires, but may also be used for pest control (fumigation), communication, defensive and offensive capabilities in the military, cooking, or smoking. It is used in rituals where incense, sage, or resin is burned to produce a smell for spiritual or magical purposes. It can also be a flavoring agent and preservative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg/330px-Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Smoke_chemical_composition.jpg/500px-Smoke_chemical_composition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Smoke_chemical_composition.jpg/500px-Smoke_chemical_composition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chemical composition distribution of volatile organic compounds released in smoke from a variety of solid fuels[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmoke_chemical_composition.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Diesel-smoke.jpg/330px-Diesel-smoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Diesel-smoke.jpg/330px-Diesel-smoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Emission of soot in the fumes of a large diesel truck, without particle filters","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiesel-smoke.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Wildfiretopanga.jpg/500px-Wildfiretopanga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Wildfiretopanga.jpg/1280px-Wildfiretopanga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Wildfiretopanga.jpg/500px-Wildfiretopanga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Smoke from a wildfire","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWildfiretopanga.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Muizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg/500px-Muizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Muizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg/1280px-Muizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Muizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg/500px-Muizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Smoke rising up from the smoldering remains of a recently extingished mountain fire in South Africa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuizenberg_Mountian_Fires_in_Cape_Town_of_2015.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Fish_processing_hub.jpg/500px-Fish_processing_hub.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://